<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S6.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Density visualization of <math id="S6.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">SEH</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S6.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">QED</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the composed distribution <math id="S6.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> induced by our mixing policy via scalarization on fragment-based molecule generation. Each distribution is estimated from 5,000 samples. We vary the weights as (a) <math id="S6.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}\propto(0.3\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}+0.7\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}})^{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">SEH</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">QED</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>32</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}\propto(0.3\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}+0.7\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}})^{32}</annotation></semantics></math> and (b) <math id="S6.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}\propto(0.7\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}+0.3\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}})^{32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>0.7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">SEH</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>0.3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">QED</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>32</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}\propto(0.7\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{SEH}}+0.3\cdot R_{\scriptscriptstyle\mathrm{QED}})^{32}</annotation></semantics></math>. </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S6.T4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results of logical operators on molecule generation tasks. We report the percentage of 5,000 samples falling into the <span id="S6.T4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">target bin</span>: for harmonic mean (<math id="S6.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math>), where all composed objectives are high; for contrast (<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.T4.m4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_markedasmath" height="8.06" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-0.81px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 8.06 8.06" width="8.06"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,8.06) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(4.03,0) translate(0,4.03)"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 -3.75 C 2.07 -3.75 3.75 -2.07 3.75 0 C 3.75 2.07 2.07 3.75 0 3.75 Z"></path><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 0 M 3.75 0 C 3.75 2.07 2.07 3.75 0 3.75 C -2.07 3.75 -3.75 2.07 -3.75 0 C -3.75 -2.07 -2.07 -3.75 0 -3.75 C 2.07 -3.75 3.75 -2.07 3.75 0 Z M 0 0"></path></g></svg></span>), where only the first objective is high.
</span></figcaption>
