<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Details</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Exact Realization for Scalarization</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove that for scalarization with <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>, our mixing rule exactly realizes the target distribution.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{A})</annotation></semantics></math> be the directed acyclic state graph of a GFlowNet with initial state <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, sink state <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, and terminating states <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}\subset\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}\subset\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For each objective <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[k]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[k]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have a pre-trained GFlowNet with forward policy <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{i,F}(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,F}(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math>, partition function <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and terminating state distribution</p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(x)=\frac{R_{i}(x)}{Z_{i}},\qquad R_{i}(x)\geq 0,\ x\in\mathcal{X}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(x)=\frac{R_{i}(x)}{Z_{i}},\qquad R_{i}(x)\geq 0,\ x\in\mathcal{X}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We write <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for the reaching probability of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,F}</annotation></semantics></math>, satisfying the recursion <a href="#S3.E2" title="In Reaching probability. ‣ 3.1 Generative Flow Networks (GFlowNets) ‣ 3 Background ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
Let the scalarization weights be <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and define</p>
<table id="A1.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}=\frac{\omega_{i}Z_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{k}\omega_{j}Z_{j}},\qquad\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}=\frac{\omega_{i}Z_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{k}\omega_{j}Z_{j}},\qquad\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Target terminating state distribution.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mixture terminating state distribution satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(x)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{k}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x)}{\sum_{j=1}^{k}\omega_{j}Z_{j}}\propto\sum_{i=1}^{k}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(x)=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{k}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x)}{\sum_{j=1}^{k}\omega_{j}Z_{j}}\propto\sum_{i=1}^{k}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Composed forward policy.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define the mixed reaching probability</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{M}(s):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{M}(s):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the composed forward policy</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\,p_{i,F}(s^{\prime}|s)\quad\text{for all }s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus\{s_{f}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s):=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\,p_{i,F}(s^{\prime}|s)\quad\text{for all }s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus\{s_{f}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> is a special case of the general mixing policy <a href="#S4.E4" title="In 4.1 Mixture of GFlowNets ‣ 4 Method ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> for scalarization with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>: since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> reduces to a weighted sum, the normalization constant simplifies to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{M}(s)=u_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{M}(s)=u_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove that <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid policy and induces the desired mixture distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Normalization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq s_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq s_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{s^{\prime}:(s\to s^{\prime})\in\mathcal{A}}p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{s^{\prime}:(s\to s^{\prime})\in\mathcal{A}}p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and the fact that each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{i,F}(\cdot|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,F}(\cdot|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability distribution,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s^{\prime}}p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s^{\prime}}p_{M,F}(s^{\prime}|s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\underbrace{\sum_{s^{\prime}}p_{i,F}(s^{\prime}|s)}_{=1}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\underbrace{\sum_{s^{\prime}}p_{i,F}(s^{\prime}|s)}_{=1}=\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last equality uses <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mixed reaching probabilities)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> be defined by <a href="#A1.E13" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>. Then <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> coincides with the reaching probability induced by <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{M}(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{M}(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{*}:(s_{*}\to s)\in\mathcal{A}}u_{M}(s_{*})\,p_{M,F}(s|s_{*})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus\{s_{0}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{*}:(s_{*}\to s)\in\mathcal{A}}u_{M}(s_{*})\,p_{M,F}(s|s_{*})\quad\forall s\in\mathcal{S}\setminus\{s_{0}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">The base case <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{M}(s_{0})=\sum_{i}v_{i}u_{i}(s_{0})=\sum_{i}v_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{M}(s_{0})=\sum_{i}v_{i}u_{i}(s_{0})=\sum_{i}v_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> follows from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s_{0})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s_{0})=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <a href="#A1.E11" title="In Setup. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>.
For <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\neq s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\neq s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, substitute <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{s_{*}}u_{M}(s_{*})\,p_{M,F}(s|s_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{s_{*}}u_{M}(s_{*})\,p_{M,F}(s|s_{*})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{*}}\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{k}v_{j}u_{j}(s_{*})\Big)\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s_{*})}{u_{M}(s_{*})}\,p_{i,F}(s|s_{*})\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{s_{*}}\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{k}v_{j}u_{j}(s_{*})\Big)\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s_{*})}{u_{M}(s_{*})}\,p_{i,F}(s|s_{*})\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}\sum_{s_{*}}u_{i}(s_{*})\,p_{i,F}(s|s_{*})=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)=u_{M}(s)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}\sum_{s_{*}}u_{i}(s_{*})\,p_{i,F}(s|s_{*})=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)=u_{M}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">using the reaching probability recursion <a href="#S3.E2" title="In Reaching probability. ‣ 3.1 Generative Flow Networks (GFlowNets) ‣ 3 Background ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in the penultimate equality.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.3</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(State distribution factorization)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For each <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, the state probability satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{i}(s)\,\rho_{i}(s)\quad\text{and}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{i}(s)\,\rho_{i}(s)\quad\text{and}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\,\rho_{M}(s)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\,\rho_{M}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>) is the probability of terminating the trajectory when at state <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i,F}</annotation></semantics></math> (resp. <math id="A1.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the standard GFlowNet factorization: the probability of being at <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> equals the probability of reaching <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> times the probability of terminating from <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. The equality for <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> follows since <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math> is a valid forward policy by Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma A.1 (Normalization). ‣ Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.4</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Correctness of the composed forward policy)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be given by <a href="#A1.E11" title="In Setup. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. Then, for all states <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(s)=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(s)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(s)=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(s).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently, the induced terminating state distribution satisfies <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x)=\sum_{i}v_{i}p_{i}(x)\propto\sum_{i}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">∝</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x)=\sum_{i}v_{i}p_{i}(x)\propto\sum_{i}\omega_{i}R_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma A.3 (State distribution factorization). ‣ Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a> and the definition of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M,F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M,F}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\,\rho_{M}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\,\rho_{M}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\,\rho_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=u_{M}(s)\sum_{i=1}^{k}\frac{v_{i}u_{i}(s)}{u_{M}(s)}\,\rho_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)\,\rho_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}u_{i}(s)\,\rho_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(s)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{i=1}^{k}v_{i}p_{i}(s),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality follows from applying <a href="#A1.E14" title="In Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> to the termination probability, and the last step uses <a href="#A1.E15" title="In Lemma A.3 (State distribution factorization). ‣ Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> for each <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Evaluating <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Theorem A.4 (Correctness of the composed forward policy). ‣ Composed forward policy. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> on terminating states <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x)=\sum_{i}v_{i}p_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x)=\sum_{i}v_{i}p_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>; substituting the definitions proves the proportionality claim via <a href="#A1.E12" title="In Target terminating state distribution. ‣ A.1 Exact Realization for Scalarization ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remarks.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(i) The result holds for any non-negative <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; they need not sum to <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>.
(ii) If estimated partition functions <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are used in place of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sampler targets the scalarized reward up to a global rescaling, which does not affect the induced distribution.
(iii) The support of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> equals the union of supports of the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>; no extra coverage assumptions are required beyond a shared state graph.
(iv) This exactness result holds specifically for scalarization with <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For general composition operators or <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the distortion factor <math id="A1.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(x)=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(x)=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> introduced in <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Analysis of the Induced Distribution ‣ 4 Method ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> characterizes the gap between the realized and target distributions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Derivation of Reaching Probability Estimator</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the reaching probability estimator and discuss how different GFlowNet training objectives affect its availability.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training objectives and model parameterization.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">GFlowNet training objectives differ in what quantities they parameterize.
Flow Matching (FM) and Detailed Balance (DB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite> explicitly parameterize the state flow <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(s)</annotation></semantics></math> for all states <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, along with the forward policy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}</annotation></semantics></math> and backward policy <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, where the partition function is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=F(s_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=F(s_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Sub-Trajectory Balance (SubTB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> similarly parameterizes the state flow <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In contrast, Trajectory Balance (TB) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> only parameterizes <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, without explicitly learning the state flow <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(s)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since our mixing rule requires the reaching probability <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be computed from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> (as we derive below), objectives that explicitly parameterize the state flow (FM, DB, SubTB) are directly compatible with our framework.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Derivation of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s)=F_{i}(s)/Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s)=F_{i}(s)/Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any state <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, the state flow <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(s)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the total flow passing through <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="F_{i}(s)=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}F_{i}(\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(s)=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}F_{i}(\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the sum is over all complete trajectories <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> that pass through <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F_{i}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F_{i}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> is the flow along trajectory <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since the total flow equals the partition function, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\tau}F_{i}(\tau)=Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\tau}F_{i}(\tau)=Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can write:</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{F_{i}(s)}{Z_{i}}=\frac{\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}F_{i}(\tau)}{\sum_{\tau}F_{i}(\tau)}=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}\frac{F_{i}(\tau)}{Z_{i}}=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}p_{i}(\tau)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>F</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>τ</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{F_{i}(s)}{Z_{i}}=\frac{\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}F_{i}(\tau)}{\sum_{\tau}F_{i}(\tau)}=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}\frac{F_{i}(\tau)}{Z_{i}}=\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}p_{i}(\tau),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(\tau)=F_{i}(\tau)/Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(\tau)=F_{i}(\tau)/Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the probability of trajectory <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By definition <a href="#S3.E1" title="In Reaching probability. ‣ 3.1 Generative Flow Networks (GFlowNets) ‣ 3 Background ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Eq.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s)=\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{s_{0},s}}p_{i}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s)=\sum_{\tau\in\mathcal{T}_{s_{0},s}}p_{i}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{s_{0},s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{s_{0},s}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the set of trajectories from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
Since the DAG structure ensures that every trajectory starting from <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> eventually reaches <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability one, this equals <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}p_{i}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\tau:s\in\tau}p_{i}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Therefore, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}(s)=F_{i}(s)/Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>F</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}(s)=F_{i}(s)/Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for all states <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Derivation of <math id="A1.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> Decomposition</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We derive the decomposition of the <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between the induced distribution <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the target distribution <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> (Eq. (<a href="#S5.Ex3" title="In 5.3 Analysis of Approximation Quality ‣ 5 Synthetic Experiments ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>) in the main text).</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> pre-trained GFlowNets with terminating distributions <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}(x)\propto R_{i}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}(x)\propto R_{i}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, recall from Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Analysis of the Induced Distribution ‣ 4 Method ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> that the distribution induced by our mixing policy takes the form:</p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x)=\frac{u_{M}(x)}{N_{M}(x)}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x)=\frac{u_{M}(x)}{N_{M}(x)}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(x):=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(x):=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the distortion factor.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The target distribution is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}^{*}(x)=\frac{\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))}{Z_{M}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}^{*}(x)=\frac{\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))}{Z_{M}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{M}=\sum_{x}\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{M}=\sum_{x}\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is the partition function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Derivation.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> distance between the induced and target distributions is:</p>
<table id="A1.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{1}=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}|p_{M}(x)-p_{M}^{*}(x)|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{1}=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}|p_{M}(x)-p_{M}^{*}(x)|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the expressions for <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{M}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{M}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|p_{M}(x)-p_{M}^{*}(x)\right|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>M</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|p_{M}(x)-p_{M}^{*}(x)\right|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\frac{u_{M}(x)}{N_{M}(x)}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\frac{u_{M}(x)}{N_{M}(x)}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Using the definition of the distortion factor <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta(x)=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta(x)=u_{M}(x)/N_{M}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\delta(x)\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\right|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\delta(x)\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> (as it is defined through non-negative reward functions and probability distributions), we can factor it out of the absolute value:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle L_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle L_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\delta(x)-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\right|\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>M</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{x\in\mathcal{X}}\left|\delta(x)-\frac{1}{Z_{M}}\right|\cdot\mathcal{G}(p_{1}(x),\ldots,p_{k}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Synthetic Experiments</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reward functions.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use five reward functions (Figure <a href="#A2.F1.sf1" title="Figure 1(a) ‣ Figure A1 ‣ Reward functions. ‣ B.1 Synthetic Experiments ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a>): Shubert, Currin, Sphere, and Branin from multi-objective optimization benchmarks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, and a Diagonal sigmoid reward. All rewards are normalized to <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. We additionally use three synthetic Circle rewards (Figure <a href="#A2.F1.sf2" title="Figure 1(b) ‣ Figure A1 ‣ Reward functions. ‣ B.1 Synthetic Experiments ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(b)</span></a>).
Each Circle reward defines a Gaussian (mixture) density inside a circular region of radius <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and assigns a constant background reward <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math> outside the circle.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F1" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F1.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.21565v1/five_reward_fns.png" id="A2.F1.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/81;" width="429" height="81" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F1.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A2.F1.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Five rewards on the <math id="A2.F1.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> grid. From left to right: Shubert, Diagonal, Currin, Sphere, and Branin.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A2.F1.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2602.21565v1/three_circle_reward_fns.png" id="A2.F1.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:281/93;" width="281" height="93" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F1.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A2.F1.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Circle rewards on the <math id="A2.F1.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> grid. From left to right: Circle1–3.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure A1</span>: </span><span id="A2.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization of reward functions on the <math id="A2.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32\times 32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32\times 32</annotation></semantics></math> grid domain used in our experiments.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scalarization (Mix-<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>).</h5>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define scalarization targets using weighted-sum rewards over a subset of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> objectives.
Table <a href="#A2.T1" title="Table A1 ‣ Scalarization (Mix-𝑘). ‣ B.1 Synthetic Experiments ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A1</span></a> lists the objective subsets used in our experiments.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A1</span>: </span><span id="A2.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Objective subsets used for Mix-<math id="A2.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> scalarization (<a href="#A2.F1.sf1" title="In Figure A1 ‣ Reward functions. ‣ B.1 Synthetic Experiments ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Details ‣ Training-free Composition of Pre-trained GFlowNets for Multi-Objective Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1(a)</span></a>).</span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T1.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T1.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T1.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_border_tt"></td>
<th id="A2.T1.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Objectives</th></tr>
<tr id="A2.T1.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T1.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Mix2</td>
<td id="A2.T1.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">Shubert, Diagonal</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T1.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T1.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Mix3</td>
<td id="A2.T1.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Shubert, Diagonal, Currin</td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T1.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T1.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Mix4</td>
<td id="A2.T1.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">Shubert, Diagonal, Currin, Sphere</td></tr>
